  "findings": [
    "Exact native max-age refusal pair is required while validity and arithmetic TTL remain valid and all other gates pass. The missing TIME_FITNESS evidence follows from that temporal gate. Old history remains unopened as current prior.",
    "The aged branch executes the existing public cold current-review contract: additional typed PURE check, fresh Root review, selected Work and current custody. Controlled future eligibility time is labelled and never advances actual Work clocks.",
    "Expired, conflict and quarantine refuse before Work. Original history bytes are compared; exact DRS record filename grammar matches native storage and reconstructs no permission.",
    "Source revision changes only the scenario document via TaskStore.register_source and the ordinary reader, retains bytes/hash/revision, then passes the old live binding to the actual G4 consumer before bootstrap.",
    "An unrelated separately admitted cold controller and Root execute real G3 PURE Work with no foreign prior; original history is compared before/after.",
    "Six owner attempts are explicitly split across two three-role rounds. Existing per-round policies, finite model selector and zero provider/effect budgets for native Work are unchanged.",
    "v02 profile path selection is consistent across entry, gate, owner bootstrap, activator, supervisor and input. Before-install pins still refer to the actual P31 predecessor; v01 was never activated.",
    "Diagnostics adds only 24 exact closed literals; source-coordinate and first-error handling behavior is unchanged.",
    "4800-second owner operation budget comprises six serial 600-second response ceilings, 900 native seconds and 300 preparation overhead; one cleanup is at most 30 seconds. These are provisional spending ceilings, not ETA or TTL changes.",
    "A separately reviewed runner/control/copy grant and exact ordinary-reader actual remain required. No new execution or owner acceptance follows from source review."
